From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:15:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read Member Voting History PDFs with native Julia code

getSession57HouseLegislativeMemberVotingHistory no longer needs Java
(JavaCall and Tabula) or the 7z program (p7zip_jll), so it no longer
needs JULIA_COPY_STACKS=1 either. Everything it needs is nested inside
the function: a Deflate decompressor, a zip reader that checks each
file's CRC-32, and a PDF text reader. It adds no dependencies.

The output for the 57th Legislature, 2nd Regular Session is identical
to the old version's: all 67,945 votes, every column. Once compiled, a
call takes about 3.3 s instead of about 70 s, or about 1.3 s when Julia
has 4 threads, as the PDFs are then read in parallel. A first call in a
Julia session, which also compiles the code, takes about 17 s instead
of about 80 s.

